---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import Stage from "../../components/Stage.astro";
---
<Base title="Disclosure and accordion" description="iVOLT disclosure and accordion: native details/summary with optional JavaScript for cancelable events and exclusive accordions.">
  <article class="docs-prose">
    <h1>Disclosure and accordion</h1>
    <p>Built on <code>&lt;details&gt;</code>, so it works without JavaScript. The optional component adds cancelable events and the <code>exclusive</code> accordion behaviour.</p>
    <p class="docs-meta"><strong>CSS:</strong> <code>css/components/disclosure.css</code>. <strong>JS (optional):</strong> <code>@intervolutions/ivolt/disclosure</code> or <code>auto.js</code>.</p>
    <Stage primary name="disclosure/basic" title="A panel that folds" />

    <Section title="Accordion" num={1}>
      <p>Several disclosures inside <code>iv-accordion</code>. With <code>data-iv-exclusive="true"</code> opening one closes its siblings.</p>
      <Stage name="disclosure/accordion" title="An accordion of disclosures" />
    </Section>

    <Section title="Options, methods, events" num={2}>
      <div class="docs-scroller">
        <table><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Attribute</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>exclusive</code></td><td><code>data-iv-exclusive</code></td><td><code>false</code></td></tr></tbody></table>
      </div>
      <p><code>open()</code>, <code>close()</code>, <code>toggle()</code>, <code>isOpen</code>, <code>destroy()</code>. Events: <code>iv:open</code> and <code>iv:close</code> (cancelable), then <code>iv:opened</code> / <code>iv:closed</code>. Cancelling a user-initiated toggle restores the previous state.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Keyboard" num={3}>
      <p>Enter or Space on the summary toggles it (native behaviour).</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Common mistakes" num={4}>
      <ul><li>Hiding essential content in a closed disclosure with no other way to reach it, such as prices or legal text.</li><li>Nesting interactive controls inside <code>&lt;summary&gt;</code>.</li></ul>
    </Section>
  </article>
</Base>
